record construction of opaque type `YieldCurve` outside its defining module `Shoals.Curves`

The four producer guards run inside `Shoals.Curves`, so they cannot see a
record literal written anywhere else. While the representation was public this
compiled, and `rate_at(curve, 1.5)` answered 0.025 for reordered pillars where
0.035 is correct -- shoals#119's exact wrong number, reached past every guard.

Opacity (`spec/02-surf-syntax.md` P16) is what makes the pillar-order rule a
property of the type rather than of four call sites: a value can only originate
from an in-module producer, and every in-module producer either runs the
strictly-increasing guard on caller-supplied times or reuses the times of a
curve that already passed it. The diagnostic lists the sanctioned producers,
which is the set of escape points that argument has to cover -- the five
sensitivity shifts appear there as `YieldCurve -> YieldCurve`, i.e. as the
inductive step. The checker verifies only that values originate in-module; that
each producer guards or passes through guarded times is a reading of the
source.
